CASE 3: Delete middle node

Input: 5 -> 10 -> 15 -> 20 -> 25
                    ^
                 del_node


BEFORE DELETION:

[5|•] -> [10|•] -> [15|•] -> [20|•] -> [25|•] -> null
                    ^
                 del_node


STEP 1: Copy next node's data

del_node.data = 20

[5|•] -> [10|•] -> [20|•] -> [20|•] -> [25|•] -> null
                    ^
                 del_node


STEP 2: Skip the next node

del_node.next = 25

[5|•] -> [10|•] -> [20|•] -----------> [25|•] -> null
                    ^                    ^
                 del_node        (orphaned [20|•])


AFTER DELETION:

[5|•] -> [10|•] -> [20|•] -> [25|•] -> null

Output: 5 -> 10 -> 20 -> 25 ✓


VISUAL EXPLANATION:

Before:
┌─────┐    ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐
│ 10  │ -> │ 20  │ -> │  4  │ -> │ 30  │ -> null
└─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘
           ↑
        del_node

Step 1 (Copy data):
┌─────┐    ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐
│ 10  │ -> │  4  │ -> │  4  │ -> │ 30  │ -> null
└─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘
           ↑
        del_node (data changed)

Step 2 (Skip next):
┌─────┐    ┌─────┐              ┌─────┐
│ 10  │ -> │  4  │ ------------>│ 30  │ -> null
└─────┘    └─────┘    ╳╳╳╳╳╳╳╳╳ └─────┘
           ↑           (deleted)
        del_node

After:
┌─────┐    ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐
│ 10  │ -> │  4  │ -> │ 30  │ -> null
└─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘


KEY INSIGHT:

Since we don't have access to the previous node, we can't unlink del_node directly.

TRICK: Instead of deleting del_node itself:
1. Copy the next node's data into del_node
2. Delete the next node instead (which we CAN do since we have del_node.next)

This effectively "replaces" del_node with its next node, achieving the same result!


CONSTRAINTS HANDLED:

✓ Guaranteed del_node is not the last node (so del_node.next always exists)
✓ Works in O(1) time - no traversal needed
✓ Works in O(1) space - no extra memory used


//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Delete without Head Pointer

Given a node del_node from a singly linked list (but NOT the head), delete this node from the list.

Constraints:
- The node to be deleted is NOT the tail node
- No head pointer is provided
- Values before and after del_node must remain in same order

Examples:

Input:  10 -> 20 -> 4 -> 30, del_node = 20
Output: 10 -> 4 -> 30

Input:  1 -> 2, del_node = 1
Output: 2

Input:  5 -> 10 -> 15 -> 20, del_node = 15
Output: 5 -> 10 -> 20

Time Complexity: O(1) - constant time operation
Space Complexity: O(1) - no extra space used

TRICK: Copy next node's data, then skip next node!
